Package: oaxaca-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, calamares, sudo, rsync, btrfs-progs, xfsprogs
# rsync: Calamares 3.3.14's unpackfs module copies the squashfs with rsync (its main.py
# always builds an UnpackOperation around "rsync -aHAXSr"); Ubuntu's calamares package does
# not depend on rsync because Ubuntu's own images get it from the standard task, which this
# minbase image does not install. Without it the install fails after partitioning with
# "rsync failed with error code 127" (seen on the Legion laptop, 2026-10-11).
# btrfs-progs, xfsprogs: partition.conf offers btrfs and xfs; mkfs.btrfs and mkfs.xfs come
# from these (ext4 and vfat tools are in the base image).
Description: Calamares settings and branding for installing Oaxaca
 The configuration that turns Ubuntu's calamares package into the Oaxaca
 installer: the module sequence (partitioning with optional LUKS, users, the
 SDDM session, GRUB with Ubuntu's signed shim, the desktop's own install-time
 setup), the branding, and a launcher that autostarts in the live session.
 Installed only in the installation ISO's squashfs; it removes itself from the
 installed system.
